    "id": "documentdb-customer-performance",
    "title": "Customer-impacting DocumentDB performance regressions",
    "what_to_watch": "Customer-impacting Amazon DocumentDB performance regressions",
    "why_watch": "Decide whether a broad database performance movement needs the DocumentDB service owner's attention.",
    "watch_for": [
      "p95 query latency is elevated across multiple regions or clusters",
      "replication lag, throttled requests, and storage pressure move with latency",
      "a recent deployment temporally precedes the correlated movement",
      "an isolated CPU spike is not sufficient evidence of broad customer impact"
    ],
    "questions": [
      "Is the impact broad across regions or clusters?",
      "Is the recent deployment a plausible common cause?",
      "Which service owner should receive the investigation?"
    ],
    "decision_guidance": "Ignore isolated CPU-only spikes or single-cluster changes. Investigate when multiple customer-impact signals move together but causation is uncertain. Notify the DocumentDB performance owner when broad impact is supported. Escalate only for confirmed widespread customer impact or failed evidence.",
